# MEGA HOTEL — COMPLETE NATIVE ANDROID FOOD DELIVERY APP

Build a complete, production-oriented native Android food delivery application for Megha Hotel, Urlabari, Morang, Nepal, using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.

The application should provide a reliable food ordering experience comparable in functionality to Foodmandu and Jaldimai, with a premium, simple, mobile-friendly interface.

This is a RESTAURANT FOOD DELIVERY APP, NOT a hotel room booking app.

## 1. Core Project Requirements

- Platform: Native Android APK.
- Language: Kotlin.
- UI: Jetpack Compose.
- Architecture: MVVM, repository pattern, and clean separation of UI, business logic, networking, and data.
- Backend: Reuse the existing Flask backend and its APIs wherever possible.
- Database: Inspect the existing database and reuse it. If the existing system uses Turso/libSQL, remain compatible with it.
- Image storage: Reuse the existing persistent image storage, such as Cloudinary, if configured.
- Currency: NPR (Rs.).
- Location: Urlabari, Morang, Nepal.
- Branding: Premium green, cream, and gold.
- Languages: English and Nepali, with a language selector.
- Customer experience: Guest ordering and authenticated customer accounts.
- Staff experience: Admin, kitchen/order staff, and delivery staff within the same APK.
- Delivery staff: Support two staff accounts, with the ability for Admin to add or deactivate staff later.
- Do not build a separate Admin website.
- Do not replace or damage the existing website or production database.
- Do not delete existing records or migrate production data destructively.
- Do not invent APIs, credentials, provider configuration, payment verification, GPS locations, or order statuses.
- Deliver functional code and backend integration, not just attractive UI mockups.

First inspect the existing backend routes, database schema, menu website, image URLs, authentication setup, and deployment configuration. Reuse working components and document anything that cannot be accessed.

