## 14. Live Google Maps Delivery Tracking

Implement real delivery tracking, not a simulated moving marker.

### Customer experience
- Display a Track Order action for an eligible active order.
- Show a Google Map with the restaurant, customer destination, and actual assigned delivery rider position.
- Display the latest rider location.
- Update the map without requiring a manual refresh.
- Show the last location update time.
- Show order status.
- Display route/polyline and ETA only when the relevant mapping and routing services are properly configured.
- If live location or ETA is unavailable, explain this honestly and display the latest known status.

### Delivery staff
- Provide a My Deliveries screen.
- Display only assigned deliveries.
- Allow staff to accept or start an authorized delivery.
- Request location permission when necessary.
- Use an Android foreground location service with a visible notification while actively sharing location, subject to Android platform requirements.
- Send real GPS coordinates to an authenticated backend at a reasonable interval, such as every 5–10 seconds when conditions and system restrictions allow.
- Stop location sharing after delivery completion, cancellation, or other defined termination conditions.
- Do not track staff outside authorized active deliveries.
- Handle denied permissions, lost GPS, poor connectivity, and battery restrictions.

### Admin
- Assign or reassign orders to the two delivery staff members.
- View the latest reported location for active deliveries.
- View assignment and delivery status.
- Restrict location access to authorized roles.

### Map configuration
- Use the official Google Maps SDK for Android.
- Document Google Cloud project configuration, Android API key restrictions, package name, signing certificate fingerprints, and any required billing or API enablement.
- Store secrets appropriately and restrict API keys.
- Do not fabricate coordinates, rider movements, or ETA.
- Ensure backend authorization prevents a customer from tracking another customer's order.

If the backend does not provide realtime delivery events, implement an appropriate authenticated polling or realtime transport strategy and document its configuration.

